IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Interpretation Act 1987 (New South Wales), Part 5 Construction of Acts and instruments: sections 31 to 38.
-- Reckoning of time (section 36(1) and (2)) and age (section 37) are computed in nsw-interpretation-time.l4.
-- Judgments the Act leaves to the reader (whether a construction would be in excess of a power, whether a report is relevant) are plain inputs.

§ `Part 5 Construction of Acts and instruments`

§§ `31 Acts and instruments to be construed so as not to exceed the legislative power of Parliament`

-- src:331 | (1) An Act or instrument shall be construed as operating to the full extent of, but so as not to exceed, the legislative power of Parliament.
@ref s 31(1) (src:331)
GIVEN `it is an Act or instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 31(1) the Act or instrument is construed as operating so as to exceed the legislative power of Parliament` MEANS
    IF `it is an Act or instrument` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:332 | (2) If any provision of an Act or instrument, or the application of any such provision to any person, subject-matter or circumstance, would, but for this section, be construed as being in excess of the legislative power of Parliament—
-- src:333 | (a) it shall be a valid provision to the extent to which it is not in excess of that power, and
@ref s 31(2)(a) (src:332-333)
GIVEN `a provision, or its application to a person, subject-matter or circumstance, would but for section 31 be construed as being in excess of the legislative power of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 31(2)(a) the provision operates to the extent to which it is not in excess of the legislative power of Parliament` MEANS
    IF `a provision, or its application to a person, subject-matter or circumstance, would but for section 31 be construed as being in excess of the legislative power of Parliament` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:332 | (2) If any provision of an Act or instrument, or the application of any such provision to any person, subject-matter or circumstance, would, but for this section, be construed as being in excess of the legislative power of Parliament—
-- src:333 | (a) it shall be a valid provision to the extent to which it is not in excess of that power, and
-- src:334 | (b) the remainder of the Act or instrument, and the application of the provision to other persons, subject-matters or circumstances, shall not be affected.
@ref s 31(2)(b) (src:332-334)
GIVEN `a provision, or its application to a person, subject-matter or circumstance, would but for section 31 be construed as being in excess of the legislative power of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 31(2)(b) the remainder of the Act or instrument, and the application of the provision to other persons, subject-matters or circumstances, is affected` MEANS
    IF `a provision, or its application to a person, subject-matter or circumstance, would but for section 31 be construed as being in excess of the legislative power of Parliament` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:335 | (3) This section applies to an Act or instrument in addition to, and without limiting the effect of, any provision of the Act or instrument.
@ref s 31(3) (src:335)
GIVEN `it is an Act or instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 31(3) section 31 applies to the Act or instrument in addition to any provision of the Act or instrument` MEANS
    IF `it is an Act or instrument` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§§ `32 Instruments to be construed so as not to exceed the powers conferred by the Acts under which they are made`

-- src:338 | (1) An instrument shall be construed as operating to the full extent of, but so as not to exceed, the power conferred by the Act under which it is made.
@ref s 32(1) (src:338)
GIVEN `it is an instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 32(1) the instrument is construed as operating so as to exceed the power conferred by the Act under which it is made` MEANS
    IF `it is an instrument` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:339 | (2) If any provision of an instrument, or the application of any such provision to any person, subject-matter or circumstance, would, but for this section, be construed as being in excess of the power conferred by the Act under which it is made—
-- src:340 | (a) it shall be a valid provision to the extent to which it is not in excess of that power, and
@ref s 32(2)(a) (src:339-340)
GIVEN `a provision of an instrument, or its application to a person, subject-matter or circumstance, would but for section 32 be construed as being in excess of the power conferred by the Act under which the instrument is made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 32(2)(a) the provision operates to the extent to which it is not in excess of the power conferred by the Act under which the instrument is made` MEANS
    IF `a provision of an instrument, or its application to a person, subject-matter or circumstance, would but for section 32 be construed as being in excess of the power conferred by the Act under which the instrument is made` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:339 | (2) If any provision of an instrument, or the application of any such provision to any person, subject-matter or circumstance, would, but for this section, be construed as being in excess of the power conferred by the Act under which it is made—
-- src:340 | (a) it shall be a valid provision to the extent to which it is not in excess of that power, and
-- src:341 | (b) the remainder of the instrument, and the application of the provision to other persons, subject-matters or circumstances, shall not be affected.
@ref s 32(2)(b) (src:339-341)
GIVEN `a provision of an instrument, or its application to a person, subject-matter or circumstance, would but for section 32 be construed as being in excess of the power conferred by the Act under which the instrument is made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 32(2)(b) the remainder of the instrument, and the application of the provision to other persons, subject-matters or circumstances, is affected` MEANS
    IF `a provision of an instrument, or its application to a person, subject-matter or circumstance, would but for section 32 be construed as being in excess of the power conferred by the Act under which the instrument is made` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:342 | (3) This section applies to an instrument in addition to, and without limiting the effect of, any provision of the instrument or of the Act under which it is made.
@ref s 32(3) (src:342)
GIVEN `it is an instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 32(3) section 32 applies to the instrument in addition to any provision of the instrument or of the Act under which it is made` MEANS
    IF `it is an instrument` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§§ `33 Regard to be had to purposes or objects of Acts and statutory rules`

-- src:345 | In the interpretation of a provision of an Act or statutory rule, a construction that would promote the purpose or object underlying the Act or statutory rule (whether or not that purpose or object is expressly stated in the Act or statutory rule or, in the case of a statutory rule, in the Act under which the rule was made) shall be preferred to a construction that would not promote that purpose or object.
@ref s 33 (src:345)
GIVEN `the first construction would promote the purpose or object underlying the Act or statutory rule` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the second construction would promote the purpose or object underlying the Act or statutory rule` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 33 the first construction is preferred to the second construction` MEANS
    IF `the first construction would promote the purpose or object underlying the Act or statutory rule` AND (NOT `the second construction would promote the purpose or object underlying the Act or statutory rule`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF (NOT `the first construction would promote the purpose or object underlying the Act or statutory rule`) AND `the second construction would promote the purpose or object underlying the Act or statutory rule`
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE NOTHING

§§ `34 Use of extrinsic material in the interpretation of Acts and statutory rules`

-- Why consideration of the material is sought. Section 34(1) names two reasons.
DECLARE ReasonForConsideringMaterial IS ONE OF
    ToConfirmThatTheMeaningIsTheOrdinaryMeaningConveyedByTheText
    ToDetermineTheMeaningOfTheProvision
    ForSomeOtherReason

-- src:348 | (1) In the interpretation of a provision of an Act or statutory rule, if any material not forming part of the Act or statutory rule is capable of assisting in the ascertainment of the meaning of the provision, consideration may be given to that material—
-- src:349 | (a) to confirm that the meaning of the provision is the ordinary meaning conveyed by the text of the provision (taking into account its context in the Act or statutory rule and the purpose or object underlying the Act or statutory rule and, in the case of a statutory rule, the purpose or object underlying the Act under which the rule was made), or
-- src:350 | (b) to determine the meaning of the provision—
-- src:351 | (i) if the provision is ambiguous or obscure, or
-- src:352 | (ii) if the ordinary meaning conveyed by the text of the provision (taking into account its context in the Act or statutory rule and the purpose or object underlying the Act or statutory rule and, in the case of a statutory rule, the purpose or object underlying the Act under which the rule was made) leads to a result that is manifestly absurd or is unreasonable.
@ref s 34(1) (src:348-352)
GIVEN `the material does not form part of the Act or statutory rule` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the material is capable of assisting in the ascertainment of the meaning of the provision` IS A BOOLEAN
      reason IS A ReasonForConsideringMaterial
      `the provision is ambiguous or obscure` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the ordinary meaning conveyed by the text leads to a result that is manifestly absurd or is unreasonable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 34(1) consideration may be given to the material in the interpretation of the provision` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the material does not form part of the Act or statutory rule` AND `the material is capable of assisting in the ascertainment of the meaning of the provision`)
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE CONSIDER reason
         WHEN ToConfirmThatTheMeaningIsTheOrdinaryMeaningConveyedByTheText THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN ToDetermineTheMeaningOfTheProvision THEN JUST (`the provision is ambiguous or obscure` OR `the ordinary meaning conveyed by the text leads to a result that is manifestly absurd or is unreasonable`)
         WHEN ForSomeOtherReason THEN NOTHING

-- The material section 34(2) says may be considered. "includes" leaves the list open.
DECLARE KindOfMaterial IS ONE OF
    AMatterSetOutInThePublishedDocumentContainingTheText
    AReportOfARoyalCommissionLawReformCommissionOrCommitteeOfInquiry
    AReportOfAParliamentaryCommittee
    ATreatyReferredToInTheAct
    AnExplanatoryNoteOrMemorandumRelatingToTheBill
    TheSecondReadingSpeech
    ADocumentDeclaredByTheActToBeRelevant
    MaterialInTheMinutesVotesOrOfficialRecordOfDebates
    SomeOtherMaterial

-- src:353 | (2) Without limiting the effect of subsection (1), the material that may be considered in the interpretation of a provision of an Act, or a statutory rule made under the Act, includes—
-- src:354 | (a) all matters not forming part of the Act that are set out in the document containing the text of the Act as published on the NSW legislation website,
-- src:355 | (b) any relevant report of a Royal Commission, Law Reform Commission, committee of inquiry or other similar body that was laid before either House of Parliament before the provision was enacted or made,
-- src:356 | (c) any relevant report of a committee of Parliament or of either House of Parliament before the provision was enacted or made,
-- src:357 | (d) any treaty or other international agreement that is referred to in the Act,
-- src:358 | (e) any explanatory note or memorandum relating to the Bill for the Act, or any other relevant document, that was laid before, or furnished to the members of, either House of Parliament by a Minister or other member of Parliament introducing the Bill before the provision was enacted or made,
-- src:359 | (f) the speech made to a House of Parliament by a Minister or other member of Parliament on the occasion of the moving by that Minister or member of a motion that the Bill for the Act be read a second time in that House,
-- src:360 | (g) any document (whether or not a document to which a preceding paragraph applies) that is declared by the Act to be a relevant document for the purposes of this section, and
-- src:361 | (h) any relevant material in the Minutes of Proceedings or the Votes and Proceedings of either House of Parliament or in any official record of debates in Parliament or either House of Parliament.
@ref s 34(2) (src:353-361)
GIVEN material IS A KindOfMaterial
      `it meets the conditions the paragraph states for it, including any requirement that it be relevant and be laid, furnished or made before the provision was enacted or made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 34(2) the material may be considered in the interpretation of the provision` MEANS
    CONSIDER material
    WHEN SomeOtherMaterial THEN NOTHING
    WHEN AMatterSetOutInThePublishedDocumentContainingTheText THEN IF `it meets the conditions the paragraph states for it, including any requirement that it be relevant and be laid, furnished or made before the provision was enacted or made` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN AReportOfARoyalCommissionLawReformCommissionOrCommitteeOfInquiry THEN IF `it meets the conditions the paragraph states for it, including any requirement that it be relevant and be laid, furnished or made before the provision was enacted or made` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN AReportOfAParliamentaryCommittee THEN IF `it meets the conditions the paragraph states for it, including any requirement that it be relevant and be laid, furnished or made before the provision was enacted or made` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN ATreatyReferredToInTheAct THEN IF `it meets the conditions the paragraph states for it, including any requirement that it be relevant and be laid, furnished or made before the provision was enacted or made` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN AnExplanatoryNoteOrMemorandumRelatingToTheBill THEN IF `it meets the conditions the paragraph states for it, including any requirement that it be relevant and be laid, furnished or made before the provision was enacted or made` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN TheSecondReadingSpeech THEN IF `it meets the conditions the paragraph states for it, including any requirement that it be relevant and be laid, furnished or made before the provision was enacted or made` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN ADocumentDeclaredByTheActToBeRelevant THEN IF `it meets the conditions the paragraph states for it, including any requirement that it be relevant and be laid, furnished or made before the provision was enacted or made` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN MaterialInTheMinutesVotesOrOfficialRecordOfDebates THEN IF `it meets the conditions the paragraph states for it, including any requirement that it be relevant and be laid, furnished or made before the provision was enacted or made` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- The matters section 34(3) names, "in addition to any other relevant matters".
DECLARE MatterToBeRegardedInWeighingMaterial IS ONE OF
    TheDesirabilityOfPersonsBeingAbleToRelyOnTheOrdinaryMeaningConveyedByTheText
    TheNeedToAvoidProlongingProceedingsWithoutCompensatingAdvantage
    SomeOtherRelevantMatter

-- src:362 | (3) In determining whether consideration should be given to any material, or in considering the weight to be given to any material, regard shall be had, in addition to any other relevant matters, to—
-- src:363 | (a) the desirability of persons being able to rely on the ordinary meaning conveyed by the text of the provision (taking into account its context in the Act or statutory rule and the purpose or object underlying the Act or statutory rule and, in the case of a statutory rule, the purpose or object underlying the Act under which the rule was made), and
-- src:364 | (b) the need to avoid prolonging legal or other proceedings without compensating advantage.
@ref s 34(3) (src:362-364)
GIVEN matter IS A MatterToBeRegardedInWeighingMaterial
      `the other matter is relevant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 34(3) regard shall be had to the matter in determining whether consideration should be given to material, or the weight to be given to it` MEANS
    CONSIDER matter
    WHEN TheDesirabilityOfPersonsBeingAbleToRelyOnTheOrdinaryMeaningConveyedByTheText THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN TheNeedToAvoidProlongingProceedingsWithoutCompensatingAdvantage THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN SomeOtherRelevantMatter THEN IF `the other matter is relevant` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§§ `34A Declaration of validity of certain laws`

-- src:367 | Each provision of an Act or statutory rule enacted or made, or purporting to have been enacted or made, before the commencement of the Australia Acts—
-- src:368 | (a) has the same effect as it would have had, and
-- src:369 | (b) is as valid as it would have been,
-- src:370 | if the Australia Acts had been in operation at the time of its enactment or making, or purported enactment or making.
@ref s 34A (src:367-370)
GIVEN `the provision of the Act or statutory rule was enacted or made, or purported to have been enacted or made, before the commencement of the Australia Acts` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 34A the provision has the same effect, and the same standing, as it would have had if the Australia Acts had been in operation at the time of its enactment or making` MEANS
    IF `the provision of the Act or statutory rule was enacted or made, or purported to have been enacted or made, before the commencement of the Australia Acts` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§§ `35 Headings etc`

-- The printed matter section 35 sorts into the part of the Act and the part that is not.
DECLARE PrintedMatter IS ONE OF
    AHeadingToAChapterPartDivisionOrSubdivision
    AHeadingToASchedule
    AHeadingToAProvisionOtherThanThose
    ParenthesisedMatterThatMerelySetsOutAHeadingToOrDescribesAnotherProvision
    AMarginalNoteFootnoteOrEndnote
    AHeadingMarginalNoteFootnoteOrEndnoteToATableOrForm
    TheNumberOfASectionSubsectionClauseOrSubclause
    SomeOtherPrintedMatter

-- src:373 | (1) Headings to provisions of an Act or instrument, being headings to—
-- src:374 | (a) Chapters, Parts, Divisions or Subdivisions into which the Act or instrument is divided, or
-- src:375 | (b) Schedules to the Act or instrument,
-- src:376 | shall be taken to be part of the Act or instrument.
-- src:377 | (2) Except as provided by subsections (3) and (4)—
-- src:378 | (a) a heading to a provision of an Act or instrument (not being a heading referred to in subsection (1)),
-- src:379 | (b) matter within a provision of an Act or instrument (being matter in parentheses that merely sets out a heading to or describes the effect of some other provision of the Act or instrument or of some other Act or instrument), or
-- src:380 | (c) a marginal note, footnote or endnote in an Act or instrument,
-- src:381 | shall be taken not to be part of the Act or instrument.
-- src:382 | (3) A heading to a provision of an Act or instrument (not being a heading referred to in subsection (1)) shall be taken to be part of the Act or instrument if, immediately before 1 February 1981 (being the date on which section 3 of the Interpretation (Amendment) Act 1980 commenced), it was part of the Act or instrument.
-- src:383 | (4) A heading to a provision of an Act or instrument (not being a heading referred to in subsection (1)), or a marginal note, footnote or endnote in an Act or instrument, shall be taken to be part of the Act or instrument if—
-- src:384 | (a) it is referred to expressly, otherwise than by means of matter within some other provision of the Act or instrument (being matter in parentheses that merely sets out a heading to or describes the effect of the firstmentioned provision) or by means of a symbol, in some other part of the Act or instrument, or
-- src:385 | (b) not being so referred to, it is a heading, marginal note, footnote or endnote to a table or form in the Act or instrument.
-- src:386 | (4A) The number of a section, subsection, clause or subclause of an Act or instrument is taken to be part of the Act or instrument even though it appears in a heading to the section, subsection, clause or subclause.
@ref s 35 (src:373-386)
GIVEN matter IS A PrintedMatter
      `immediately before 1 February 1981 it was part of the Act or instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is referred to expressly in some other part of the Act or instrument, otherwise than by parenthesised matter that merely sets out a heading to or describes the effect of the provision or by means of a symbol` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 35 the printed matter is taken to be part of the Act or instrument` MEANS
    CONSIDER matter
    WHEN AHeadingToAChapterPartDivisionOrSubdivision THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN AHeadingToASchedule THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN AHeadingToAProvisionOtherThanThose THEN JUST (`immediately before 1 February 1981 it was part of the Act or instrument` OR `it is referred to expressly in some other part of the Act or instrument, otherwise than by parenthesised matter that merely sets out a heading to or describes the effect of the provision or by means of a symbol`)
    WHEN ParenthesisedMatterThatMerelySetsOutAHeadingToOrDescribesAnotherProvision THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN AMarginalNoteFootnoteOrEndnote THEN JUST `it is referred to expressly in some other part of the Act or instrument, otherwise than by parenthesised matter that merely sets out a heading to or describes the effect of the provision or by means of a symbol`
    WHEN AHeadingMarginalNoteFootnoteOrEndnoteToATableOrForm THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN TheNumberOfASectionSubsectionClauseOrSubclause THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN SomeOtherPrintedMatter THEN NOTHING

-- src:387 | (5) This section does not limit the application of section 34 in relation to the use of any heading, marginal note, footnote or endnote in the interpretation of the provision to which the heading, marginal note, footnote or endnote relates.
@ref s 35(5) (src:387)
GIVEN `the use is in the interpretation of the provision to which the heading, marginal note, footnote or endnote relates` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 35 limits the application of section 34 to the use of the heading, marginal note, footnote or endnote` MEANS
    IF `the use is in the interpretation of the provision to which the heading, marginal note, footnote or endnote relates` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

§§ `36 Reckoning of time`

-- Subsections (1) and (2) are computed in nsw-interpretation-time.l4.
-- src:395 | (3) If in any Act or instrument a period of time is prescribed or allowed for the doing of any thing and a power is conferred on any person or body to extend the period of time—
-- src:396 | (a) that power may be exercised, and
-- src:397 | (b) if the exercise of that power depends on the making of an application for an extension of the period of time—such an application may be made,
-- src:398 | after the period of time has expired.
@ref s 36(3)(a) (src:395-398)
GIVEN `a period of time is prescribed or allowed for the doing of a thing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a power is conferred on a person or body to extend the period of time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the period of time has expired` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 36(3)(a) the power to extend the period may be exercised after the period has expired` MEANS
    IF `a period of time is prescribed or allowed for the doing of a thing` AND `a power is conferred on a person or body to extend the period of time`
    THEN IF `the period of time has expired` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:395 | (3) If in any Act or instrument a period of time is prescribed or allowed for the doing of any thing and a power is conferred on any person or body to extend the period of time—
-- src:396 | (a) that power may be exercised, and
-- src:397 | (b) if the exercise of that power depends on the making of an application for an extension of the period of time—such an application may be made,
-- src:398 | after the period of time has expired.
@ref s 36(3)(b) (src:395-398)
GIVEN `a period of time is prescribed or allowed for the doing of a thing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a power is conferred on a person or body to extend the period of time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the exercise of the power depends on the making of an application for an extension` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the period of time has expired` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 36(3)(b) the application for an extension of the period may be made after the period has expired` MEANS
    IF `a period of time is prescribed or allowed for the doing of a thing` AND `a power is conferred on a person or body to extend the period of time` AND `the exercise of the power depends on the making of an application for an extension`
    THEN IF `the period of time has expired` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `37 Age`

-- Computed in nsw-interpretation-time.l4 as `s 37 the moment a person attains an age in years`.

§§ `38 Measurement of distance`

DECLARE PurposeOfMeasuringDistance IS ONE OF
    AnActPassedBeforeTheCommencementOfThisAct
    AnInstrumentMadeUnderAnActPassedBeforeTheCommencementOfThisAct
    AnActPassedAfterTheCommencementOfThisAct
    AnInstrumentMadeUnderAnActPassedAfterTheCommencementOfThisAct
    SomeOtherPurposeOfMeasuringDistance

DECLARE WayOfMeasuringDistance IS ONE OF
    AlongTheNearestRouteOrdinarilyUsedInTravelling
    InAStraightLineOnAHorizontalPlane

-- src:404 | In the measurement of any distance—
-- src:405 | (a) for the purposes of any Act passed before the commencement of this Act, or any instrument made under such an Act, the distance shall be measured according to the nearest route ordinarily used in travelling, and
-- src:406 | (b) for the purposes of any Act passed after the commencement of this Act, or any instrument made under such an Act, the distance shall be measured in a straight line on a horizontal plane.
@ref s 38 (src:404-406)
GIVEN purpose IS A PurposeOfMeasuringDistance
GIVETH A MAYBE WayOfMeasuringDistance
`s 38 the way the distance is measured` MEANS
    CONSIDER purpose
    WHEN AnActPassedBeforeTheCommencementOfThisAct THEN JUST AlongTheNearestRouteOrdinarilyUsedInTravelling
    WHEN AnInstrumentMadeUnderAnActPassedBeforeTheCommencementOfThisAct THEN JUST AlongTheNearestRouteOrdinarilyUsedInTravelling
    WHEN AnActPassedAfterTheCommencementOfThisAct THEN JUST InAStraightLineOnAHorizontalPlane
    WHEN AnInstrumentMadeUnderAnActPassedAfterTheCommencementOfThisAct THEN JUST InAStraightLineOnAHorizontalPlane
    WHEN SomeOtherPurposeOfMeasuringDistance THEN NOTHING

§§ `Tests: Part 5`

-- s 31
#ASSERT `s 31(1) the Act or instrument is construed as operating so as to exceed the legislative power of Parliament` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 31(1) the Act or instrument is construed as operating so as to exceed the legislative power of Parliament` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 31(2)(a) the provision operates to the extent to which it is not in excess of the legislative power of Parliament` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 31(2)(a) the provision operates to the extent to which it is not in excess of the legislative power of Parliament` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 31(2)(b) the remainder of the Act or instrument, and the application of the provision to other persons, subject-matters or circumstances, is affected` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 31(2)(b) the remainder of the Act or instrument, and the application of the provision to other persons, subject-matters or circumstances, is affected` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 31(3)
#ASSERT `s 31(3) section 31 applies to the Act or instrument in addition to any provision of the Act or instrument` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 31(3) section 31 applies to the Act or instrument in addition to any provision of the Act or instrument` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 32
#ASSERT `s 32(3) section 32 applies to the instrument in addition to any provision of the instrument or of the Act under which it is made` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 32(3) section 32 applies to the instrument in addition to any provision of the instrument or of the Act under which it is made` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 32(1) the instrument is construed as operating so as to exceed the power conferred by the Act under which it is made` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 32(1) the instrument is construed as operating so as to exceed the power conferred by the Act under which it is made` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 32(2)(a) the provision operates to the extent to which it is not in excess of the power conferred by the Act under which the instrument is made` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 32(2)(a) the provision operates to the extent to which it is not in excess of the power conferred by the Act under which the instrument is made` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 32(2)(b) the remainder of the instrument, and the application of the provision to other persons, subject-matters or circumstances, is affected` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 32(2)(b) the remainder of the instrument, and the application of the provision to other persons, subject-matters or circumstances, is affected` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 33: preferred only where one construction promotes the purpose and the other does not
#ASSERT `s 33 the first construction is preferred to the second construction` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 33 the first construction is preferred to the second construction` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 33 the first construction is preferred to the second construction` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 33 the first construction is preferred to the second construction` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 34(1): material that is part of the Act is outside; (a) confirm; (b) determine only on ambiguity or absurdity
#ASSERT `s 34(1) consideration may be given to the material in the interpretation of the provision` TRUE TRUE ToConfirmThatTheMeaningIsTheOrdinaryMeaningConveyedByTheText FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 34(1) consideration may be given to the material in the interpretation of the provision` TRUE TRUE ToDetermineTheMeaningOfTheProvision TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 34(1) consideration may be given to the material in the interpretation of the provision` TRUE TRUE ToDetermineTheMeaningOfTheProvision FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 34(1) consideration may be given to the material in the interpretation of the provision` TRUE TRUE ToDetermineTheMeaningOfTheProvision FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 34(1) consideration may be given to the material in the interpretation of the provision` TRUE FALSE ToConfirmThatTheMeaningIsTheOrdinaryMeaningConveyedByTheText TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
